WEBVTT

1
00:00:01,368 --> 00:00:02,469
[Chopping wood]

2
00:00:03,403 --> 00:00:04,739
What's wrong with that thing?

3
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:06,774
It's the signal.

4
00:00:07,709 --> 00:00:09,074
I think.

5
00:00:09,076 --> 00:00:10,576
Why don't you put that
thing down and look at nature

6
00:00:10,578 --> 00:00:12,179
through your own
eyes for a change?

7
00:00:12,614 --> 00:00:13,748
[Birds, nature sounds]

8
00:00:14,248 --> 00:00:15,449
How's that dinner coming?

9
00:00:16,149 --> 00:00:18,586
I'm wasting away over here.

10
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:21,054
Maybe if you helped,
you'd be eating already.

11
00:00:21,455 --> 00:00:22,322
I'll help.

12
00:00:22,657 --> 00:00:23,723
Okay. Thanks, sweetheart.

13
00:00:23,725 --> 00:00:24,489
Come here.

14
00:00:24,491 --> 00:00:25,292
Careful of the fire.

15
00:00:25,459 --> 00:00:26,528
I know, mom.

16
00:00:29,196 --> 00:00:30,430
[Fire crackling]

17
00:00:37,104 --> 00:00:39,439
Uh, as long as you girls are
helping, I could use a hand

18
00:00:39,607 --> 00:00:40,407
over here.

19
00:00:41,241 --> 00:00:44,344
I am not chopping wood.

20
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:48,415
Like I would trust
you with an axe.

21
00:00:49,149 --> 00:00:49,751
Whatever.

22
00:00:50,718 --> 00:00:51,617
Seriously. Phone down.

23
00:00:51,619 --> 00:00:52,654
The fire needs more wood.

24
00:00:57,725 --> 00:00:58,526
Thanks, kiddo.

25
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:02,062
[Sudden boom]

26
00:01:03,497 --> 00:01:04,732
[Ominous music]

27
00:01:05,198 --> 00:01:06,099
You gotta help me.

28
00:01:06,668 --> 00:01:08,703
Please. No, listen, listen.

29
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:09,671
He's gone crazy.

30
00:01:09,837 --> 00:01:10,736
He's going crazy.

31
00:01:10,738 --> 00:01:11,671
We have to get out of here.

32
00:01:11,673 --> 00:01:12,640
All of us, we have to...

33
00:01:12,807 --> 00:01:13,608
There's no time.

34
00:01:15,208 --> 00:01:16,143
[Gunshot]

35
00:01:16,511 --> 00:01:17,545
[Scream]

36
00:01:17,712 --> 00:01:19,479
Get back! Please,
over here, here.

37
00:01:21,148 --> 00:01:21,683
You okay?

38
00:01:23,283 --> 00:01:23,751
Fuck!

39
00:01:26,588 --> 00:01:27,287
Shit!

40
00:01:28,856 --> 00:01:29,724
Put it down.

41
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:31,091
Put it down!

42
00:01:31,491 --> 00:01:33,126
Okay, okay.

43
00:01:33,293 --> 00:01:34,294
Move away from the axe.

44
00:01:34,629 --> 00:01:36,163
[Music intensifying]

45
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:37,130
It's okay.

46
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:41,168
Is there a road nearby?

47
00:01:41,803 --> 00:01:42,402
What?

48
00:01:42,604 --> 00:01:43,705
A road!

49
00:01:43,871 --> 00:01:44,639
That way.

50
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:49,577
Give me your keys.

51
00:01:50,511 --> 00:01:51,445
Your keys!

52
00:01:52,179 --> 00:01:52,714
Now!

53
00:01:58,385 --> 00:01:58,820
Please.

54
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:00,755
It's okay.

55
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:04,291
Look,

56
00:02:05,492 --> 00:02:06,661
I wasn't gonna hurt you.

57
00:02:06,828 --> 00:02:08,896
Jesus. Did he touch you?

58
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:10,865
Did he touch you?

59
00:02:11,231 --> 00:02:12,232
No. He just ran past.

60
00:02:12,399 --> 00:02:13,200
He didn't hurt her.

61
00:02:13,735 --> 00:02:16,169
I swear... he didn't.

62
00:02:16,671 --> 00:02:17,404
It's okay.

63
00:02:17,639 --> 00:02:18,673
[Music dies down]

64
00:02:18,873 --> 00:02:19,473
Please.

65
00:02:20,908 --> 00:02:21,542
It's okay.

66
00:02:23,778 --> 00:02:24,444
I'm sorry.

67
00:02:25,245 --> 00:02:26,179
No!

68
00:02:32,787 --> 00:02:34,454
[Jet engine sounds]

69
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:04,451
[Shaking sound]

70
00:03:06,754 --> 00:03:08,488
[Clicking, static]

71
00:03:14,261 --> 00:03:15,697
Man's bag is his life.

72
00:03:17,264 --> 00:03:18,231
Don't mess with that.

73
00:03:18,766 --> 00:03:20,501
I didn't touch your bag, man.

74
00:03:22,302 --> 00:03:24,804
'Cause the last time some
asshole put a scorpion in my

75
00:03:24,806 --> 00:03:26,440
bag to try and scare me.

76
00:03:27,842 --> 00:03:29,977
That's an awful thing to do.

77
00:03:31,813 --> 00:03:33,514
How childish.

78
00:03:34,247 --> 00:03:37,685
Scorpions in each other's bags,
pissing in each other's beers.

79
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:39,954
When will it end?

80
00:03:40,822 --> 00:03:41,589
Enjoy your beer.

81
00:03:43,323 --> 00:03:44,992
[Turbulance]

82
00:03:45,893 --> 00:03:47,394
Uh, almost got it on my shirt.

83
00:03:48,730 --> 00:03:49,764
Could you even tell?

84
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:52,397
Bite me.

85
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:55,235
I guess three mill' doesn't
go far these days, hey?

86
00:03:55,837 --> 00:03:57,404
I don't think that's
the plane, though.

87
00:03:58,673 --> 00:04:00,307
Everything all right
up there, boss?

88
00:04:03,376 --> 00:04:04,979
Approach. X-ray
X-ray November.

89
00:04:05,345 --> 00:04:05,813
Say again.

90
00:04:07,648 --> 00:04:09,584
[Dials clicking]

91
00:04:10,852 --> 00:04:12,852
Approach. This is X-ray
X-ray November.

92
00:04:12,854 --> 00:04:13,621
Come in.

93
00:04:15,957 --> 00:04:17,424
[Plane rattles]

94
00:04:17,859 --> 00:04:18,793
Is it turbulence?

95
00:04:19,861 --> 00:04:21,028
No, I think it's electrical.

96
00:04:22,029 --> 00:04:23,396
[Tense music]

97
00:04:24,599 --> 00:04:26,366
You're not gonna
crash again, are you?

98
00:04:28,970 --> 00:04:30,972
Approach X-ray X-ray November.

99
00:04:36,043 --> 00:04:37,912
Approach. This is X-ray
X-ray November.

100
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:38,880
Do you read?

101
00:04:41,481 --> 00:04:42,717
X-ray X-ray November.

102
00:04:42,884 --> 00:04:43,918
Clear to land.

103
00:04:45,352 --> 00:04:47,989
All right, ladies,
stow your seats

104
00:04:48,355 --> 00:04:49,991
and leave it the
way you found it.

105
00:04:51,759 --> 00:04:53,561
[Computer warning, "Burn out"]

106
00:04:53,928 --> 00:04:55,428
["Engine failure"]

107
00:04:58,498 --> 00:05:00,034
[Computer warning continues]

108
00:05:07,508 --> 00:05:09,744
[Ominous music intensifying]

109
00:05:12,613 --> 00:05:14,314
["Engine failure"]

110
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:15,850
[Warning alarms]

111
00:05:21,354 --> 00:05:22,924
X-ray X-ray November.

112
00:05:24,559 --> 00:05:25,858
Foxtrot X-ray X-ray November.

113
00:05:25,860 --> 00:05:26,826
Radar contact.

114
00:05:26,828 --> 00:05:29,864
Beware ILF operative
visual left traffic.

115
00:05:32,633 --> 00:05:33,968
Should get lower
a little bit here.

116
00:05:49,349 --> 00:05:51,719
[Computer warning
"Terrain, terrain, pull up"]

117
00:06:02,563 --> 00:06:04,397
[Warning alarms continue]

118
00:06:10,504 --> 00:06:11,839
[Tire screech]

119
00:06:16,577 --> 00:06:19,680
[Military theme music]

120
00:06:39,967 --> 00:06:42,603
[Military music continues]

121
00:06:49,043 --> 00:06:52,046
[Jet engines wind down]

122
00:07:18,005 --> 00:07:19,040
Thanks for the ride, Pete.

123
00:07:19,206 --> 00:07:19,941
Stay out of trouble.

124
00:07:20,641 --> 00:07:21,075
Always.

125
00:07:25,046 --> 00:07:28,215
[Music fades]

126
00:07:34,588 --> 00:07:35,254
Good to see you.

127
00:07:35,256 --> 00:07:37,058
You too, Mac. How's Susan?

128
00:07:38,059 --> 00:07:38,826
Sir?

129
00:07:40,594 --> 00:07:41,662
Right.

130
00:07:41,829 --> 00:07:43,463
We're on the
clock here, Dallas.

131
00:07:46,534 --> 00:07:47,868
How's the flight?

132
00:07:48,069 --> 00:07:49,937
Like this...
the closer we got.

133
00:07:50,538 --> 00:07:51,806
Which is fine for you here,

134
00:07:51,973 --> 00:07:53,908
but when you're 20,000 feet
in the air it's...

135
00:07:54,842 --> 00:07:56,544
...gonna go over there.

136
00:07:58,846 --> 00:08:00,548
Is that why we're here
instead of Wainwright?

137
00:08:02,650 --> 00:08:03,483
It's part of it.

138
00:08:07,021 --> 00:08:09,857
[People chatter]

139
00:08:20,668 --> 00:08:22,169
Show them.

140
00:08:25,172 --> 00:08:28,741
12 days ago, a UAP appeared out
of nowhere over our airspace,

141
00:08:28,743 --> 00:08:29,910
traveling at over Mach five.

142
00:08:30,244 --> 00:08:31,443
Approximately 30 seconds
after that

143
00:08:31,445 --> 00:08:34,682
it suddenly lost
altitude and came down here.

144
00:08:35,983 --> 00:08:37,084
Did you bring it down?

145
00:08:37,518 --> 00:08:39,585
No. We scrambled C-130s
and fast movers

146
00:08:39,587 --> 00:08:41,922
over the search
area and found the wreckage.

147
00:08:42,089 --> 00:08:44,656
We recovered what we could
and set up a secure site in a

148
00:08:44,658 --> 00:08:46,794
nearby abandoned mine here.

149
00:08:48,162 --> 00:08:49,096
Why?

150
00:08:49,597 --> 00:08:51,165
Let me guess, E.M. interference?

151
00:08:51,699 --> 00:08:53,532
It wreaks havoc with
instruments and electrical

152
00:08:53,534 --> 00:08:54,635
the closer you get.

153
00:08:54,902 --> 00:08:56,203
We couldn't fly it out.

154
00:08:56,637 --> 00:08:58,871
Luckily, we had an old logging
truck to ferry it

155
00:08:58,873 --> 00:09:00,608
to the makeshift lab.

156
00:09:00,975 --> 00:09:01,709
What is it?

157
00:09:02,676 --> 00:09:03,809
We think it's a...

158
00:09:03,811 --> 00:09:06,614
It's an experimental
Russian aircraft. Nothing more.

159
00:09:08,983 --> 00:09:09,917
Who the hell are you?

160
00:09:10,651 --> 00:09:11,752
I'm the guy paying you.

161
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:13,854
Spook central.

162
00:09:14,755 --> 00:09:15,823
What's going on, Mac?

163
00:09:17,058 --> 00:09:18,926
The mine shielded
the interference

164
00:09:19,093 --> 00:09:20,995
until eight hours ago
when this happened.

165
00:09:22,129 --> 00:09:24,999
[Computer analysing sounds]

166
00:09:28,702 --> 00:09:29,835
That's not right.

167
00:09:29,837 --> 00:09:31,639
The satellite's just
a really fancy camera high up.

168
00:09:31,806 --> 00:09:32,704
Localized E.M.

169
00:09:32,706 --> 00:09:34,608
wouldn't jank the
images like this.

170
00:09:34,775 --> 00:09:35,910
Doesn't change the facts.

171
00:09:36,143 --> 00:09:38,079
No signals in or out.

172
00:09:38,579 --> 00:09:40,181
Can't even get a
bird to fly over it.

173
00:09:40,714 --> 00:09:42,983
Over 70 personnel
working 'round the clock.

174
00:09:43,617 --> 00:09:45,953
Haven't heard from a single
one of them since it went dark.

175
00:09:46,187 --> 00:09:48,322
Whatever's happening
it's getting bigger.

176
00:09:48,689 --> 00:09:50,758
Nearest town's Neandeg about
40 miles from the mine.

177
00:09:50,925 --> 00:09:51,959
It's already getting affected.

178
00:09:52,126 --> 00:09:53,327
This is above our pay grade.

179
00:09:54,361 --> 00:09:55,729
What do you need us to do?

180
00:09:56,864 --> 00:09:58,933
Our on site lead is
Doctor Moira Knight.

181
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:01,635
Basically an
astrophysics expert.

182
00:10:01,836 --> 00:10:02,935
[Whistle]

183
00:10:02,937 --> 00:10:05,106
If Hynek were alive, he'd
have her on speed dial.

184
00:10:05,306 --> 00:10:06,874
Someone just got a hard on.

185
00:10:07,041 --> 00:10:08,142
Oh, bro, you got no idea.

186
00:10:08,309 --> 00:10:10,175
Go in,
get her personal hard drive

187
00:10:10,177 --> 00:10:11,745
and engage
the kill switch.

188
00:10:12,613 --> 00:10:13,981
It's a fail safe for the lab.

189
00:10:14,148 --> 00:10:16,715
Triggers a series of explosions
that buries the mine and

190
00:10:16,717 --> 00:10:17,818
whatever is inside it.

191
00:10:18,752 --> 00:10:20,054
What about Doctor Knight?

192
00:10:20,654 --> 00:10:23,224
SOP was to evac the moment
anything went sideways.

193
00:10:24,391 --> 00:10:26,994
So that means anyone left
inside is considered hostile.

194
00:10:27,161 --> 00:10:28,129
Got it?

195
00:10:29,897 --> 00:10:31,799
We all have our orders, Dallas.

196
00:10:32,199 --> 00:10:32,967
Copy that.

197
00:10:33,701 --> 00:10:34,635
Any questions?

198
00:10:35,836 --> 00:10:37,204
I suppose you're coming with us.

199
00:10:37,638 --> 00:10:38,672
Do I look retarded?

200
00:10:40,641 --> 00:10:41,942
You look like an asshole.

201
00:10:43,077 --> 00:10:43,844
What was that?

202
00:10:44,845 --> 00:10:45,978
I said, why us?

203
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:46,845
Taylor!

204
00:10:46,847 --> 00:10:47,913
No, man.

205
00:10:47,915 --> 00:10:50,684
We get sent in when
people need to be rescued.

206
00:10:51,318 --> 00:10:52,386
Or need to disappear.

207
00:10:53,087 --> 00:10:55,289
This is neither, save or grave.

208
00:10:55,823 --> 00:10:58,425
Because everything we're
talking about is paid for by an

209
00:10:58,792 --> 00:10:59,725
appropriations bill

210
00:10:59,727 --> 00:11:01,128
that has nothing to
do with any of it.

211
00:11:01,762 --> 00:11:03,397
None of us are even
here right now.

212
00:11:03,931 --> 00:11:05,065
Plausible deniability.

213
00:11:05,699 --> 00:11:07,201
So why not just use
a kinetic strike?

214
00:11:07,368 --> 00:11:09,069
Bury it under the mountain?

215
00:11:09,370 --> 00:11:12,004
The information stuck on that
hard drive represents a global

216
00:11:12,006 --> 00:11:13,941
shift for whoever can
get their hands on it.

217
00:11:14,108 --> 00:11:17,242
Uncle Sam wants it, and he's
going to be very generous when

218
00:11:17,244 --> 00:11:18,045
he gets it.

219
00:11:18,946 --> 00:11:19,880
So get to work.

220
00:11:21,182 --> 00:11:22,917
The clock is ticking, Gentlemen.

221
00:11:23,817 --> 00:11:25,819
Are you in or out?

222
00:11:33,727 --> 00:11:36,130
[Energetic rock music]

223
00:11:45,739 --> 00:11:48,008
[Water splashing]

224
00:12:01,855 --> 00:12:03,891
[Road noise]

225
00:12:24,011 --> 00:12:26,146
[Humvee rush by sound]

226
00:12:29,216 --> 00:12:30,918
Blackhog Base
this is Blackhog One.

227
00:12:31,185 --> 00:12:32,384
Traveling toward crossing

228
00:12:32,386 --> 00:12:34,755
six... northing

229
00:12:35,122 --> 00:12:36,890
on... break.

230
00:12:37,791 --> 00:12:38,957
What road is this?

231
00:12:38,959 --> 00:12:43,130
Damned if I know, just tell him
we're on highway three.

232
00:12:43,297 --> 00:12:45,533
Past the offshoot
to Morris Lake.

233
00:12:45,899 --> 00:12:46,798
Blackhog One, uh

234
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,168
...on the offshoot
past Morris Lake.

235
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:50,836
Copy, Blackhog One.

236
00:12:50,838 --> 00:12:52,206
Continue to the next waypoint.

237
00:12:52,406 --> 00:12:53,207
Copy?

238
00:12:55,276 --> 00:12:57,545
[Rock music intensifies]

239
00:13:00,214 --> 00:13:01,782
[Radio] "Blackhog One, copy?"

240
00:13:02,283 --> 00:13:03,350
[Radio voice choppy]

241
00:13:03,784 --> 00:13:05,553
Blackhog Base
this is Blackhog One

242
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:06,753
Say again all,

243
00:13:06,755 --> 00:13:09,056
you're broken and unreadable.

244
00:13:09,223 --> 00:13:10,124
Over.

245
00:13:10,991 --> 00:13:12,159
They said this would happen.

246
00:13:13,127 --> 00:13:14,795
Okay, I'm still not
clear on this.

247
00:13:15,129 --> 00:13:17,896
If we're in such a hurry to get
there, why are we wasting so

248
00:13:17,898 --> 00:13:18,832
much time driving?

249
00:13:19,099 --> 00:13:20,500
Because if we took
a, uh,

250
00:13:20,502 --> 00:13:22,970
plane in, we'd crash,
you dumb fuck!

251
00:13:24,171 --> 00:13:26,440
Oh, I'm the dumb fuck.

252
00:13:27,041 --> 00:13:28,909
You're half Native
and half Polish.

253
00:13:29,143 --> 00:13:31,544
The last time you locked your
keys in your car, it took you

254
00:13:31,546 --> 00:13:33,080
an hour to get your family out.

255
00:13:34,815 --> 00:13:35,449
What do you call

256
00:13:35,816 --> 00:13:36,649
an East Indian

257
00:13:36,651 --> 00:13:38,452
not trying to sell
you something?

258
00:13:38,919 --> 00:13:39,521
What?

259
00:13:39,887 --> 00:13:41,322
A surprise!

260
00:13:41,589 --> 00:13:42,821
Surprise...

261
00:13:42,823 --> 00:13:44,958
I'm surprised you
remembered the punch line.

262
00:13:45,125 --> 00:13:46,827
I'm also surprised you
could deliver that joke

263
00:13:46,994 --> 00:13:48,395
in less than three hours.

264
00:13:48,563 --> 00:13:51,063
Would you two shit heads
please keep it down?

265
00:13:51,065 --> 00:13:51,999
I'm trying to read.

266
00:13:52,199 --> 00:13:53,867
(Both)
Shut the fuck up!

267
00:13:55,135 --> 00:13:56,268
All right.

268
00:13:56,270 --> 00:13:58,038
There should be an old
logging road just up ahead.

269
00:13:59,139 --> 00:14:00,074
Got it.

270
00:14:01,008 --> 00:14:04,011
[Music continues]

271
00:14:18,025 --> 00:14:19,093
So..

272
00:14:20,027 --> 00:14:21,228
What's with you and
cats, anyway?

273
00:14:21,495 --> 00:14:22,394
What can I say?

274
00:14:22,396 --> 00:14:24,298
They're nature's
perfect killing machine.

275
00:14:24,932 --> 00:14:27,101
They're silent,
agile and deadly.

276
00:14:27,267 --> 00:14:29,468
